1
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:34,000
August 1, 1966, was the day our innocence was shattered.

2
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:02,000
Tower is a animation, crime, documentary film directed by Keith Maitland.

3
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Combining archival footage with rotoscopic animation, Tower reveals the action-packed untold stories of the witnesses, heroes and
survivors of America’s first mass school shooting, when the worst in one man brought out the best in so many others.

4
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:58,000
Claire Wilson James, played by Violett Beane.

5
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:26,000
Allen Crum, played by Chris Doubek.

6
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:54,000
Houston McCoy, played by Blair Jackson.

7
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:22,000
Ramiro "Ray" Martinez, played by Louie Arnette.

8
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:50,000
Rita Starpattern, played by Josephine McAdam.

9
00:49:12,000 --> 00:49:18,000
Aleck Hernandez Jr., played by Aldo Ordoñez.

10
00:54:40,000 --> 00:54:46,000
Tower is a 2016 American mostly-animated documentary film about the 1966 shootings at the
University of Texas at Austin directed and produced by Keith Maitland.

11
01:00:08,000 --> 01:00:14,000
The film follows the shooting from the perspectives of several survivors, recreating
their recounts via actors filmed and later animated in rotoscoping.

12
01:05:36,000 --> 01:05:42,000
The film premiered on March 13, 2016, at South by Southwest, before receiving a
limited release by Kino Lorber in the United States on September 28, 2016.

13
01:11:04,000 --> 01:11:10,000
It was later aired on television on the PBS series Independent Lens.

14
01:16:32,000 --> 01:16:38,000
The film explores themes of violence in schools,
massacre, adult animation, school shooting.
